[h1]Overview:[/h1]
Brings back the automated diplomat system from EU4 with auto-improve relations and other features.

Requires [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3692202776]Community Mod Framework (CMF)[/url].

[h1]Features:[/h1]
[olist]
 [*][b]Auto-Improve Relations:[/b]
  [list]
   [*][b]Neighboring Countries:[/b] Improves relations with random bordering nations.
   [*][b]Own Subjects:[/b] Improves relations with random subject nations.
   [*][b]Outraged Countries:[/b] Improves relations with nations that have at least 10 antagonism towards you, most antagonistic first, and cancels the improve once their antagonism drops below 5.
   [*][b]Allies:[/b] Improves relations with allied nations and defensive league members.
   [*][b]Threatening Countries:[/b] Improves relations with nations that pose the highest threat level to you first.
   [*][b]HRE Imperial Circle Leaders:[/b] Improves relations with the leaders of Imperial Circles in the Holy Roman Empire. Only visible for HRE members.
   [*][b]HRE Electors:[/b] Improves relations with Holy Roman Empire electors. Only visible for HRE members.
   [*][b]HRE Members:[/b] Improves relations with fellow Holy Roman Empire members. Only visible for HRE members.
   [*][b]Market Owners:[/b] Improves relations with countries that own a market.
   [*][b]Kingdoms and Empires:[/b] Improves relations with kingdoms and empires.
   [*][b]Largest Nations:[/b] Improves relations with the largest nations within your diplomatic range that you have discovered, starting with the biggest.
  [/list]
  [list]
   [*][b]Drag-to-Reorder Priority:[/b] Set which categories get diplomats first via the Community Mod Menu.
   [*][b]Per-Category Diplomat Limits:[/b] Control how many diplomats each category can use (0-10).
  [/list]
 [*][b]Subject Interactions:[/b] Automatically perform subject actions whenever possible.
  [list]
   [*][b]Enforce Religion:[/b] Enforce your state religion on subjects.
   [*][b]Enforce Culture:[/b] Enforce your primary culture on subjects.
  [/list]
 [*][b]Diplomat Reserves:[/b] Set a minimum number of free diplomats and minimum monthly diplomat gain to keep in reserve. Autonomous actions will not dip below your thresholds.
 [*][b]Improvement Limits:[/b] Set a maximum relations value at which improving stops and in-progress improvements are cancelled, and a maximum antagonism above which countries are skipped.
 [*][b]Block Specific Countries:[/b] Stop auto-improving relations with a chosen country using the Block Auto-Improve diplomatic action, and resume with Allow Auto-Improve.
[/olist]

[h1]Change Log:[/h1]
See the [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/changelog/$item-id$]Change Notes on the workshop page[/url].

[h1]Known Issues:[/h1]
[list]
 [*]Some diplomatic interactions won't have confirmations when they otherwise would. This is necessary for auto-cancel, but I will look into a better workaround.
[/list]

[h1]Compatibility:[/h1]
[list]
 [*]Ironman and Achievement Compatible.
 [*]Fully save game compatible.
 [*]Should work with any mod.
 [*]I may add compatibility patches upon request.
[/list]

In addition to the comment section, you can also ask any questions, report bugs, or make suggestions by pinging @arealconner in the [url=https://discord.gg/zeQ6x9wrPq]#utility-mods channel of the EU5 Community discord server[/url]. And if you are interested in joining in the development of this or one of my other mods, you can ping or add me on Discord @arealconner. All contributions are welcome.

The source and dev versions of the mod are available on [url=https://github.com/conner-olsen/eu5-autonomous-diplomats]GitHub.[/url]

